generation tools share one validation prelude: parameters, Mermaid\"},{\"line\":23,\"text\":\"// fences, workspace selection, local image references, and the structural\"},{\"line\":24,\"text\":\"// phase of step validation, with every issue aggregated into a single\"},{\"line\":25,\"text\":\"// INVALID_PROPOSAL response. It lives here once, so each new check is\"},{\"line\":26,\"text\":\"// inserted once instead of once per tool.\"},{\"line\":27,\"text\":\"//\"},{\"line\":28,\"text\":\"// Changes Tour step validation is two-phase by nature: the structure of a\"},{\"line\":29,\"text\":\"// proposal is checked here, and its anchors are staged against the analyzed\"},{\"line\":30,\"text\":\"// commit only after the caller has resolved the Git comparison (HEAD match,\"},{\"line\":31,\"text\":\"// base resolution, merge-base). Those Git checks answer with their own tool\"},{\"line\":32,\"text\":\"// error codes (STALE_HEAD, INVALID_BASE_REF, ...), so they stay in the tool\"},{\"line\":33,\"text\":\"// handler and the handler sequences the phases — but the staging order\"},{\"line\":34,\"text\":\"// itself (commit anchors, then declared baseFile values against the detected\"},{\"line\":35,\"text\":\"// renames) lives in `stageCommitAnchors`, not in the caller.\"},{\"line\":36,\"text\":\"\"},{\"line\":37,\"text\":\"export type TourProposalKind = \\\"project\\\" | \\\"changes\\\";\"},{\"line\":38,\"text\":\"\"},{\"line\":39,\"text\":\"// A rejection is already the error payload of the tool response (the shared\"},{\"line\":40,\"text\":\"// ErrorResult shape), so a handler relays it without re-deriving messages or\"},{\"line\":41,\"text\":\"// issue lists.\"}],\"nextLine\":42,\"truncatedLines\":[]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2681,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not s