{"level":30,"time":1794927894703,"pid":17869,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b71919ce-02ba-4e90-a7e9-3419110301bb","event":"trace","trace":{"type":"tool","name":"readLines","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9447f01ed0a6f563","parameters":{"endLine":1003,"file":"server.ts","startLine":860},"result":{"result":{"file":"server.ts","start":860,"lines":[{"line":860,"text":"    includesLocalChanges,"},{"line":861,"text":"  });"},{"line":862,"text":"  if (staged.issues.length > 0) {"},{"line":863,"text":"    return errorResponse("},{"line":864,"text":"      \"INVALID_PROPOSAL\","},{"line":865,"text":"      \"The create_changes_tour arguments are invalid.\","},{"line":866,"text":"      staged.issues"},{"line":867,"text":"    );"},{"line":868,"text":"  }"},{"line":869,"text":"  if ("},{"line":870,"text":"    (await committedDiffIsEmpty(ctx, mergeBaseSha, headRef)) &&"},{"line":871,"text":"    (!includeUncommittedChanges || uncommitted.length === 0)"},{"line":872,"text":"  ) {"},{"line":873,"text":"    return errorResponse("},{"line":874,"text":"      \"NO_CHANGES\","},{"line":875,"text":"      `No committed changes between the merge-base of ${baseRef} (${mergeBaseSha}) and ${headRef}. The previous tour file was preserved.`"},{"line":876,"text":"    );"},{"line":877,"text":"  }"},{"line":878,"text":""},{"line":879,"text":"  // Uncommitted changes are excluded by default with a warning, or explicitly"},{"line":880,"text":"  // included; in that case the Tour has no `ref` and reports that the result"},{"line":881,"text":"  // describes a non-reproducible local state."},{"line":882,"text":"  const warnings: Warning[] = [];"},{"line":883,"text":"  if (includesLocalChanges) {"},{"line":884,"text":"    warnings.push({"},{"line":885,"text":"      code: \"UNCOMMITTED_CHANGES_INCLUDED\","},{"line":886,"text":"      message:"},{"line":887,"text":"        \"Uncommitted changes were explicitly included; the tour describes a local state that is not reproducible from Git.\","},{"line":888,"text":"    });"},{"line":889,"text":"  } else if (uncommitted.length > 0) {"},{"line":890,"text":"    warnings.push({"},{"line":891,"text":"      code: \"UNCOMMITTED_CHANGES_EXCLUDED\","},{"line":892,"text":"      message: `${uncommitted.length} uncommitted change(s) were excluded from the analysis (staged, unstaged or untracked).`,"},{"line":893,"text":"    });"},{"line":894,"text":"  }"},{"line":895,"text":""},{"line":896,"text":"  const finalSteps = staged.steps.map((step) => {"},{"line":897,"text":"    const { display, baseFile, ...ordinaryStep } = step;"},{"line":898,"text":"    if (includesLocalChanges || step.file === undefined) return ordinaryStep;"},{"line":899,"text":"    const file = path.posix.normalize(normalizeSlashes(step.file));"},{"line":900,"text":"    return { ...ordinaryStep, file, display: \"diff\" as const, baseFile: staged.renames.get(file) };"},{"line":901,"text":"  });"}],"nextLine":902,"truncatedLines":[]},"returned":1,"observed":null,"truncated":false,"bounds":{"maxItems":50,"maxBytes":8000},"bytes":2636,"revision":"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780","provenance":"primitive-derived","uncertainty":["Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence."]},"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"usageMissing":false,"outcome":"keys=result,returned,observed,truncated","runId":"b71919ce-02ba-4e90-a7e9-3419110301bb","seq":22,"startedAt":"2026-11-17T15:04:54.474Z","endedAt":"2026-11-17T15:04:54.703Z","durationMs":229}}
{"level":30,"time":1794927894704,"pid":17869,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b71919ce-02ba-4e90-a7e9-3419110301bb","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Identifier la déclaration de create_project_tour dans server.ts (~ligne 693) et son rôle : recevoir une proposition, la faire valider, puis l'enregistrer.\",\"Délimiter le périmètre : suivre uniquement les appels indispensables au flux proposition → validation → enregistrement, en citant les numéros de lignes.\",\"Noter que le catalogue est vide : aucune fonction réutilisable connue, l'exploration reposera sur la lecture directe de server.ts.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Lire server.ts autour de la ligne 693 pour capturer la signature de create_project_tour, ses paramètres (proposition, contexte) et sa valeur de retour.\",\"Repérer dans le corps de create_project_tour l'appel de validation (ex. validate_proposal ou équivalent) et noter sa ligne exacte, ses arguments et le traitement de son résultat (erreurs, rejet).\",\"Repérer l'appel d'enregistrement/persistance (ex. save_tour, write file, store) déclenché après validation réussie, et noter sa ligne exacte et les données transmises.\",\"Vérifier s'il existe des étapes intermédiaires indispensables (transformation de la proposition, construction de l'objet tour) entre validation et enregistrement, avec leurs lignes.\",\"Identifier les limites : gestion d'erreurs partielle, validation déléguée à une fonction non lue, effets de bord non visibles depuis server.ts, dépendances externes non tracées.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclude when the evidence is sufficient. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans server.ts, comment create_project_tour reçoit-il une proposition et la fait-il valider et enregistrer ? Commence à la déclaration vers la ligne 693, suis uniquement les appels indispensables et cite leurs lignes ; signale les limites."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b088e56c70780255","type":"function","function":{"name":"readAround","arguments":"{\"file\":\"server.ts\",\"line\":693}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6af4a60bdac0157","type":"function","function":{"name":"searchIdentifiers","arguments":"{\"identifier\":\"create_project_tour\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b088e56c70780255","content":"{\"result\":{\"file\":\"server.ts\",\"start\":688,\"lines\":[{\"line\":688,\"text\":\"      ],\"},{\"line\":689,\"text\":\"    })\"},{\"line\":690,\"text\":\"  );\"},{\"line\":691,\"text\":\"\"},{\"line\":692,\"text\":\"  server.registerTool(\"},{\"line\":693,\"text\":\"    \\\"create_project_tour\\\",\"},{\"line\":694,\"text\":\"    {\"},{\"line\":695,\"text\":\"      description: PROJECT_TOUR_DESCRIPTION,\"},{\"line\":696,\"text\":\"      inputSchema: projectToolInputSchema,\"},{\"line\":697,\"text\":\"      outputSchema: toolResultSchema,\"},{\"line\":698,\"text\":\"    },\"}]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":497,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6af4a60bdac0157","content":"{\"result\":[{\"file\":\"server.ts\",\"line\":47,\"text\":\"// MCP V1 exposes exactly two tools: `create_project_tour` and\"},{\"file\":\"server.ts\",\"line\":85,\"text\":\"  \\\"Generation prompt for the create_project_tour tool: the instructions the \\\" +\"},{\"file\":\"server.ts\",\"line\":120,\"text\":\"  \\\"Generation prompt for the create_project_tour tool, composed for one \\\" +\"},{\