 du fichier cible).\",\"Vérifier si des options d'écriture sont utilisées (flag 'wx', fsync, mode) et si le rename écrase silencieusement une cible existante.\",\"Identifier les limites : pas de verrou inter-processus, pas de fsync avant rename (risque sur crash système), fenêtre de course si plusieurs processus écrivent simultanément, comportement dépendant de la plateforme.\",\"Consulter les appelsants de writeTourAtomic et les tests éventuels pour confirmer le comportement observé et les cas limites traités.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclude when the evidence is sufficient. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans persistence.ts, comment writeTourAtomic protège-t-elle le fichier cible lors de l’écriture ? Lis les lignes 13 à 53, cite les sources, et indique les limites."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a634d14e53da86","type":"function","function":{"name":"readLines","arguments":"{\"endLine\":53,\"file\":\"persistence.ts\",\"startLine\":13}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8bc646c26792b9d","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a634d14e53da86","content":"{\"result\":{\"file\":\"persistence.ts\",\"start\":13,\"lines\":[{\"line\":13,\"text\":\"export async function writeTourAtomic(\"},{\"line\":14,\"text\":\"  ctx: WorkspaceContext,\"},{\"line\":15,\"text\":\"  relativeTarget: string,\"},{\"line\":16,\"text\":\"  content: string\"},{\"line\":17,\"text\":\"): Promise<void> {\"},{\"line\":18,\"text\":\"  const target = path.resolve(ctx.root, relativeTarget);\"},{\"line\":19,\"text\":\"  const directory = path.dirname(target);\"},{\"line\":20,\"text\":\"  await fs.promises.mkdir(directory, { recursive: true });\"},{\"line\":21,\"text\":\"\"},{\"line\":22,\"text\":\"  let realDirectory: string;\"},{\"line\":23,\"text\":\"  try {\"},{\"line\":24,\"text\":\"    realDirectory = fs.realpathSync(directory);\"},{\"line\":25,\"text\":\"  } catch (error) {\"},{\"line\":26,\"text\":\"    throw new OutputPathError(\"},{\"line\":27,\"text\":\"      `Unable to resolve the output directory: ${(error as Error).message}`\"},{\"line\":28,\"text\":\"    );\"},{\"line\":29,\"text\":\"  }\"},{\"line\":30,\"text\":\"  const relative = path.relative(ctx.realRoot, realDirectory);\"},{\"line\":31,\"text\":\"  if (relative.startsWith(\\\"..\\\") || path.isAbsolute(relative)) {\"},{\"line\":32,\"text\":\"    throw new OutputPathError(\"},{\"line\":33,\"text\":\"      `${relativeTarget} resolves outside the workspace root`\"},{\"line\":34,\"text\":\"    );\"},{\"line\":35,\"text\":\"  }\"},{\"line\":36,\"text\":\"\"},{\"line\":37,\"text\":\"  const realTarget = path.join(realDirectory, path.basename(target));\"},{\"line\":38,\"text\":\"  const tempFile = path.join(\"},{\"line\":39,\"text\":\"    realDirectory,\"},{\"line\":40,\"text\":\"    `.${path.basename(target)}.tmp-${process.pid}-${Date.now()}`\"},{\"line\":41,\"text\":\"  );\"},{\"line\":42,\"text\":\"  const handle = await fs.promises.open(tempFile, \\\"w\\\");\"},{\"line\":43,\"text\":\"  try {\"},{\"line\":44,\"text\":\"    await handle.writeFile(content, \\\"utf8\\\");\"},{\"line\":45,\"text\":\"    await handle.sync();\"},{\"line\":46,\"text\":\"  } finally {\"},{\"line\":47,\"text\":\"    await handle.close();\"},{\"line\":48,\"text\":\"  }\"},{\"line\":49,\"text\":\"  try {\"},{\"line\":50,\"text\":\"    await fs.promises.rename(tempFile, realTarget);\"},{\"line\":51,\"text\":\"  } catch (error) {\"},{\"line\":52,\"text\":\"    await fs.promises.unlink(tempFile).catch(() => undefined);\"},{\"line\":53,\"text\":\"    throw error;\"}],\"nextLine\":null,\"truncatedLines\":[]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2217,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8bc646c26792b9d","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/.memory/b6f7ac2cdf7e9cfd6f12eaffefc3ebd7676d1e8405d5890db286e7a71df9299e.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/findSymbolOccurrences.ts\",\".tours/config.json\",\"cli.ts\",\"codetour-schema.ts\",\"context.ts\",\"git.ts\",\"image-validation.ts\",\"main.ts\",\"mermaid-