{"level":30,"time":1794928123377,"pid":23742,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"391d42e6-807a-4ab1-9de6-be9aa740b6b7","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"traceFunctionAndCallers","question":"How is the function {functionName} in {file} (lines {startLine}-{endLine}) implemented, and where is it called from, with exact line citations?","description":"Reproduces and extends the evidence pattern used for this objective: it reads the exact line range of a function definition in a given file, searches for all occurrences of the function's identifier to establish callers and import sites, and reads a configurable window of context lines around a known caller line in the caller file. Parameters: file (path of the defining file), functionName (identifier to search), startLine/endLine (definition range to cite), callerFile (file containing a known call site), callerLine (line of that call site), callerContextLines (radius of context lines to read around the call site, default 3). Output: an object with three fields — definition (verbatim lines of the function body), references (all syntactic occurrences of the identifier across the workspace), and callerContext (verbatim lines surrounding the call site). Limits: provides syntactic evidence only, not semantic certainty or proof of absence; requires the caller line to be known in advance (only one caller window is returned; other callers appear only in the references list); line ranges are clamped to start at line 1 but are not validated against file length; does not resolve imports, types, or runtime behavior.","source":"const traceFunctionAndCallers = async function (params: { file: string; functionName: string; startLine: number; endLine: number; callerFile: string; callerLine: number; callerContextLines?: number }): Promise<{ definition: unknown; references: unknown; callerContext: unknown }> { const contextRadius = params.callerContextLines === undefined ? 3 : par